# Build context hygiene. This shapes the IMAGE; the upload allowlist in
# scripts/package-appstore.sh shapes the ZIP. Two separate contracts.
.git
.github
.claude
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
var
data
dist
build
*.egg-info
docs
tests
*.zip
# The interface's own test suite and its fixtures. `ui/` ships - it IS the served interface - but
# its tests are not runtime and the image stays lean: no test tooling in the shipped layer, which
# is the same rule `requirements-runtime.txt` holds for pip packages. The suite still reaches the
# UPLOAD artefact, where the platform's pytest run ignores it, and a contract test holds both
# halves so the image cannot start carrying a harness by accident.
ui/tests
# Workstation scripts. `tools/udl_characterise.py` reads real UDL credentials and runs on the
# networked workstation, per the flight plan: "Runs on the networked workstation, never in the
# container." Excluded from the image context here and from the upload allowlist in
# scripts/package-appstore.sh, with a contract test holding both.
tools

# Design canvas working files. Versioned, reviewable, and never shipped: the packaging
# allowlist in scripts/package-appstore.sh names only src tests scripts docs content ui .github,
# so this is belt and braces for the image build context.
design
